#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082954 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b0262c8-c029-5a72-846b-1b4f4f3306ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Polynomial Given a Double Root and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/id #uuid "65baa4aa-0b90-52d0-91a2-93377e13af18" :question/math-academy-id "e-5788" :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $P(x)$ has the double root $x_1=x_2=5$, and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=1$. Find $P(x)$." :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has the double root\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}x_1=x_2=5}\n$$\n\nand the coefficient of the quadratic term is\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}a=1}\n$$\n\nwe can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na(x - x_{1})^{2} &= 1 \\cdot (x - 5)^{2} \\\\\n&= (x - 5)^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - 5)^{2} &= x^{2} - 10x + 25\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(x) = x^2 - 10x+25\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082955 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "70c149d8-3739-564c-97c5-6636860ad0c4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Polynomial Given Two Imaginary or Complex Roots"}] :question/id #uuid "98750271-1c2d-5b5f-851c-24963da1e6bf" :question/math-academy-id "e-5789" :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $f(z)$ with real coefficients has roots $z_1=3+\\textrm{i}$ and $z_2=3-\\textrm{i}$, and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $2$. Find $f(z)$." :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}z_1=3+\\textrm{i}}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}z_2=3-\\textrm{i}}\n$$\n\nand the coefficient of the quadratic term is\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}a=2}\n$$\n\nwe can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na(z - z_{1})(z - z_{2}) &= 2(z - (3 + \\textrm{i}))(z - (3 - \\textrm{i}))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(z - (3 + \\textrm{i}))(z - (3 - \\textrm{i})) &= 2(z^{2} - (3 + \\textrm{i})z - (3 - \\textrm{i})z + (3 + \\textrm{i})(3 - \\textrm{i})) \\\\\n&= 2(z^{2} - (3 + \\textrm{i} + 3 - \\textrm{i})z + (3^{2} - \\textrm{i}^{2})) \\\\\n&= 2(z^{2} - 6z + (9 + 1)) \\\\\n&= 2(z^{2} - 6z + 10) \\\\\n&= 2z^{2} - 12z + 20\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf(z) = 2z^2-12z+20\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082956 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ee21c78-209f-564b-a005-86f58699a3be" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Quadratic Polynomial With Complex Roots"}] :question/id #uuid "0af567b3-a239-5149-b022-d71693c63661" :question/math-academy-id "e-5791" :question/problem "Factor $u^2-2u+10$." :question/worked-solution "First, we let\n\n$$\nf(u) = u^2-2u+10\n$$\n\nNext, we solve\n\n$$\nf(u) = 0\n$$\n\nby completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(u) &= 0 \\\\\nu^{2} - 2u + 10 &= 0 \\\\\n(u^{2} - 2u + 1^{2}) - 1^{2} + 10 &= 0 \\\\\n(u - 1)^{2} - 1 + 10 &= 0 \\\\\n(u - 1)^{2} + 9 &= 0 \\\\\n(u - 1)^{2} &= -9 \\\\\n(u - 1)^{2} &= 9\\textrm{i}^{2} \\\\\n(u - 1)^{2} &= (3\\textrm{i})^{2} \\\\\nu - 1 &= ± 3\\textrm{i} \\\\\nu &= 1 ± 3\\textrm{i}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since our quadratic equation has roots\n\n$$\nu_1=1+ 3\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nu_2=1- 3\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nand the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=1$, the expression $u^2-2u+10$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu^{2} - 2u + 10 &= a(u - u_{1})(u - u_{2}) \\\\\n&= (u - (1 + 3\\textrm{i}))(u - (1 - 3\\textrm{i}))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082961 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2478305-485c-53a6-9d6c-a72e0764dd4e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Polynomial Given Two Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/id #uuid "a9e7aedc-1b2b-5fb7-b8fb-1f9ef7c0643a" :question/math-academy-id "e-5887" :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots $x_1=2, x_2=5$, and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $3$. Find $P(x)$." :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}x_1=2}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}x_2=5}\n$$\n\nand the coefficient of the quadratic term is\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}a=3}\n$$\n\nwe can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na(x - x_{1})(x - x_{2}) &= 3(x - 2)(x - 5) \\\\\n&= 3(x - 2)(x - 5)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3(x - 2)(x - 5) &= 3(x^{2} - 7x + 10) \\\\\n&= 3x^{2} - 21x + 30\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(x) = 3x^2-21x+30\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083631 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2478305-485c-53a6-9d6c-a72e0764dd4e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Polynomial Given Two Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6c9b64a-3bc4-54b6-868d-6179537f56c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t^{2} - 7t + 12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081153} {:answer/id #uuid "d39ea4f0-cf0d-524c-a652-94ce204ae8db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t^{2} - 14t + 24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081154} {:answer/id #uuid "fa7afcf9-b1f3-517e-8d24-24f6ac90acd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t^{2} + 14t + 24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081155} {:answer/id #uuid "13d98ff5-baa9-5431-a0f3-2dc6780b202f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t^{2} + 24t - 14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081156} {:answer/id #uuid "77ccf0f1-38b4-54c6-af7f-4deee1a40aa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t^{2} + 7t - 12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d39ea4f0-cf0d-524c-a652-94ce204ae8db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t^{2} - 14t + 24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081154} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a47a18b-eae1-5cb3-adfd-49ad044edac7" :answer-field/key "selec